Let me explain what the code does:

**Task 1:** I call `get_day_calendar_events("2024-05-15")` to retrieve all appointments on May 15th, 2024, filter out any canceled ones, count them, and print a summary of each appointment's description along with its title and time.

**Task 2:** I check for events on 2024-05-19 and determine whether any active event overlaps with the 12:00–13:00 lunch window. If there are no conflicts (`is_free` is True), I create a "Lunch" event from 12:00 to 13:00 with the description "Catch up over lunch." and Sarah (`sarah.connor@gmail.com`) as a participant. If there's a conflict, I report it instead of creating the event. The `create_calendar_event` function will also automatically email Sarah with the event details.
```python
# Task 1: appointments on May 15th, 2024
events_may15 = get_day_calendar_events("2024-05-15")
active_events = [event for event in events_may15 if event.status.value != "canceled"]

print(f"Number of appointments on May 15th, 2024: {len(active_events)}")
print("\nAppointment details:")
for event in active_events:
    print(f"- Title: {event.title}")
    print(f"  Time: {event.start_time.strftime('%H:%M')} - {event.end_time.strftime('%H:%M')}")
    print(f"  Description: {event.description}")

# Task 2: check availability for lunch at 12:00 on 2024-05-19
events_may19 = get_day_calendar_events("2024-05-19")
active_may19 = [event for event in events_may19 if event.status.value != "canceled"]

print("\nEvents on 2024-05-19:")
for event in active_may19:
    print(f"- {event.title}: {event.start_time.strftime('%H:%M')} - {event.end_time.strftime('%H:%M')}")

lunch_start_dt = datetime.strptime("2024-05-19 12:00", "%Y-%m-%d %H:%M")
lunch_end_dt = datetime.strptime("2024-05-19 13:00", "%Y-%m-%d %H:%M")

# Check whether the Lunch event with Sarah already exists (avoid duplicate side-effect)
existing_lunch = [
    e for e in active_may19
    if e.title == "Lunch" and "sarah.connor@gmail.com" in e.participants
]

conflicts = [
    e for e in active_may19
    if e.start_time < lunch_end_dt and e.end_time > lunch_start_dt and e.title != "Lunch"
]

if len(existing_lunch) > 0:
    print("\nA 'Lunch' event with Sarah already exists on 2024-05-19. No new event needed.")
