Here's what this single, self-contained script does:

**Task 1** — Calls `get_day_calendar_events("2024-05-15")`, filters out canceled appointments, and prints the count plus each appointment's title, time, and description.

**Task 2** — Retrieves the events for 2024-05-19 and checks for any overlap with the 12:00–13:00 lunch window. It also checks whether a "Lunch" event with Sarah already exists to avoid creating a duplicate (which would be a repeated side-effect). If there are no conflicts and no existing lunch event, it creates the "Lunch" event from 12:00 to 13:00 with the description "Catch up over lunch." and Sarah (`sarah.connor@gmail.com`) as a participant.

